Blocked by the ENF-23 gsd-test clean-tree gate: this gsd-test dispatch is piped into another command. A shell pipeline exits with the status of its LAST command, so a failed gsd-test run piped into `tail`/`tee`/`grep` reads as exit 0 — a false green.

Re-run it one of these ways:
  1. run it unpiped: `gsd-test ...` on its own;
  2. prefix the pipeline with `set -o pipefail;` so the pipeline fails when gsd-test fails;
  3. redirect to a file and read the log after: `gsd-test ... > gsd-test.log 2>&1`, then inspect `gsd-test.log` and the exit status.
